# Trivy vulnerability suppressions.
# Every entry here must have a matching write-up in SECURITY.md and a
# matching entry in .grype.yaml.
# Format: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# History: the base image was node:24.19.0-slim (Debian) through 2026-08-09,
# switched to node:24.19.0-alpine the same day after a side-by-side scan
# showed 152 findings on slim vs 11 on alpine (0 HIGH/CRITICAL either way).
# Stripping the bundled npm CLI from the runtime image (never invoked there)
# fixed the remaining fixable ones. The Debian-specific entries this file
# used to carry (util-linux, perl-base, ncurses, gzip, libacl, zlib) no
# longer apply on Alpine and were removed rather than left stale.

# CVE-2025-60876: BusyBox wget HTTP request-splitting via CRLF injection
# Severity: Medium (CVSS 6.5) — Package: busybox / busybox-binsh / ssl_client
# No fix version published yet as of 2026-08-09.
# Hestia never invokes wget or any busybox applet — the container's only
# process is `node server.js` (see Dockerfile CMD).
# exp: 2026-09-20
CVE-2025-60876
